Natas 21 → 22 — OverTheWire

Objective

The goal of this level is to log in as an administrator and retrieve the credentials for Natas 22.

The page initially reports:

You are logged in as a regular user.

The level also provides an important hint:

This website is colocated with natas21-experimenter.

The main Natas 21 page contains:

<?php

function print_credentials() {
    if($_SESSION and array_key_exists("admin", $_SESSION) and $_SESSION["admin"] == 1) {
        print "You are an admin. The credentials for the next level are:<br>";
        print "<pre>Username: natas22\n";
        print "Password: <censored></pre>";
    } else {
        print "You are logged in as a regular user. Login as an admin to retrieve credentials for natas22.";
    }
}

session_start();
print_credentials();

?>

The important part is:

$_SESSION["admin"] == 1

Therefore, the objective is to get the server to load a session containing:

admin = 1

There is no functionality on this page that actually sets the admin session variable, so I investigated the experimenter application.

2. Inspecting the Experimenter

The experimenter contains the following logic:

session_start();

if(array_key_exists("submit", $_REQUEST)) {
    foreach($_REQUEST as $key => $val) {
        $_SESSION[$key] = $val;
    }
}

This is the vulnerable section.

The application iterates through every parameter supplied in the request and copies it directly into the session.

For example, sending:

admin=1

causes:

$_SESSION["admin"] = "1";

The submit parameter is also important because it causes the vulnerable foreach loop to execute.
